ZN504XG-D voice enablement: register the Le9643 SLIC sound card node
at root level in the board DTS and turn on the AN7581 AFE.

This patch lives in dts-patches/ (applied to the OpenWrt target tree),
NOT kernel-patches/: target dts files are compiled in place from
target/linux/airoha/dts (DEVICE_DTS_DIR := ../dts) and never enter the
kernel source tree, so a kernel-series patch can never reach them.

The sound-slic node is a child of the root node, a sibling of the leds
node.  The original draft placed it inside the gpio-leds node, where
of_platform would never populate it as a platform device.

SLIC control-plane wiring (SPI bus, reset/INT GPIO pin numbers) is not
yet confirmed from schematics; this patch only brings up the ASoC side
so the AFE PCM path can be validated.  The slic-le9643 SPI node will be
added to this DTS once the pinout is known.

Signed-off-by: ZN504XG-D voice porting project
--- a/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi
@@ -101,6 +101,14 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	sound-slic {
+		compatible = "airoha,an7581-slic-sound";
+
+		platform {
+			sound-dai = <&afe>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	/* The USB PHY 3.3V reference supply is always on. */
 	reg_3p3v: regulator-3p3v {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
@@ -401,3 +409,7 @@
 	airoha,pon-data-path;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&afe {
+	status = "okay";
+};
